N1 (2026-11-10T17:08:33Z), before any training: storage only, not a method change. The dense per-position atom tensors (15 GB per raw, disk 96 % full) are replaced by a table of the 62 distinct residue graphs plus per-position graph ids. The graph layers are residue-local, so the encoder computes the same values. The dense files were deleted (derived files, from this session).
N2 (2026-11-10T17:09:08Z): the ported ReDeeM W template has 10 C, real Trp has 11. The indole six-ring is drawn with 5 atoms in redeem chemistry.rs. Kept faithful to ReDeeM, as requested. It applies equally to targets and decoys. All other 19 residues and C+CAM / M+Ox match the heavy-atom formulas.
N3 (2026-11-10T21:48:42Z): the laptop suspended (s2idle) 2026-11-10T17:09:53 to 21:47:24 local during DS11-raw01 fold 0. The process was paused, not restarted. Wall-clock times in train_DS11_raw01.log include about 4.6 h of suspend. Results are not affected.
N4 (2026-11-10T22:10:22Z): compute only, not a method change. The first chain (untrimmed, 5 s per step) was stopped by PID before any fold finished, and no scores were written. train_seq.py now encodes each distinct precursor once per batch, in length buckets trimmed to the longest peptide. Padding is masked, so values match the padded encoder (checked: max diff 2.7e-7 codes, 1.5e-7 embeddings). Folds run as separate processes, 6 threads each, and are merged afterwards. Seeds are unchanged (100+k, 200+10k+r). Only the dropout random stream differs from a single-process run.
N5 (2026-11-10T23:25:30Z): added one progress print per fit() (logging only) for the runs launched after DS11-raw01.
N6 (2026-11-11T01:16:20Z): compute only. The 3 parallel folds (6 threads each) ran about 50x slower (15 s per step, against 0.3 s for one process with 10 threads on this 6P+8E i7-1370P). They were stopped by PID after 3 h, before any fold finished, and no scores were written. Now one process at a time with OMP_NUM_THREADS=10, folds run in order inside the process. Method, seeds and the merge are unchanged.
I1 (2026-11-11T04:51:08Z), interim observation only (the verdict needs both raws, chain not changed). raw01 DS11 against D11: N@FDP_c 0.5/1/1.5/2% = 1318/1449/1513/1544 against 1256/1348/1496/1572. q<=0.01 1423 at FDP_c 0.010 against 1504 at 0.015. Entrapment AUC 0.509 against 0.511. Null-winner AUC 0.5016 against 0.5015 (rule 2 holds). Rule 3 (N@2% above control) is not met on raw01 (1544 < 1572). The gain is at the strict end (0.5-1%) only.
